# Spider-Man, Web-Slinger: "Web-slinging {W} (You may cast this spell for {W} if you also return a tapped creature you
# control to its owner's hand.)" (CR 702.188a). Both Ornithopters have attacked and are tapped in Bot1's second main
# phase of turn 5. Bot1 casts Spider-Man for {W} (a Plains) by web-slinging; only its own Ornithopter may be returned,
# not Bot2's, also tapped. Spider-Man enters, and Bot1's Ornithopter goes back to hand.

[Bot1 Deck]
Plains
Ornithopter
Spider-Man, Web-Slinger
Plains x17

[Bot2 Deck]
Island
Ornithopter
Island x18

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Plains.Play
Bot1.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Attack(Ornithopter > Bot2)
[T4 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Attack(Ornithopter > Bot1)
[T5 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Attack(Ornithopter > Bot2)
[T5 Bot1.Main2]
? Bot2.Battlefield.Ornithopter.Tapped = true
Bot1.Hand.Spider-Man, Web-Slinger.Cast(Ability: Web-slinging)
Bot1.Battlefield.Plains.Activate
! Bot1.Choose(Bot2.Battlefield.Ornithopter)
Bot1.Choose(Pay mana)
Bot1.Choose(Bot1.Battlefield.Ornithopter)
[T5 Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Turn = 5
Stack.Count = 0
Bot1.Battlefield = Plains; Spider-Man, Web-Slinger
Bot1.Hand.Count = 7
Bot2.Battlefield = Ornithopter
Bot2.Battlefield.Ornithopter.Tapped = true
